WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.960
In daylight, you can read small print.

2
00:00:03.010 --> 00:00:05.120
Every letter is sharp.

3
00:00:05.170 --> 00:00:07.850
Under the stars, you can make out shapes:

4
00:00:07.900 --> 00:00:09.710
a path, a tree.

5
00:00:09.760 --> 00:00:11.360
But not the words.

6
00:00:11.410 --> 00:00:15.060
Step into a dark room, and
at first you see little.

7
00:00:15.110 --> 00:00:18.700
Over about 20 to 30 minutes, more appears.

8
00:00:18.750 --> 00:00:21.370
So why can you read
small print in daylight,

9
00:00:21.420 --> 00:00:24.190
but only make out shapes by starlight?

10
00:00:24.240 --> 00:00:27.370
In this mission, you'll
build the eye layer by layer,

11
00:00:27.420 --> 00:00:29.650
and find each part on a slide.

12
00:00:29.700 --> 00:00:33.670
Then you'll see how the lens changes
shape to focus on something near,

13
00:00:33.720 --> 00:00:35.240
then far away.

14
00:00:35.290 --> 00:00:39.270
Your mission: explain why you
can read small print in daylight,

15
00:00:39.320 --> 00:00:41.800
but only make out shapes by starlight.
